# =============================================================================
# C3PO local config. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values below.
# `.env` is gitignored. The token is read server-side only and never sent to
# the browser.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_TOKEN — GitHub Personal Access Token (classic)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create one at: https://github.com/settings/tokens/new
#
# Recommended settings on the creation page:
#   Note:        c3po-local         (or anything memorable)
#   Expiration:  90 days            (GitHub default; renew when it lapses)
#
# Scopes to tick (classic PAT):
#   [x] read:project   Required. Projects v2 fields (Status, Priority, Size,
#                      items) only exist in GraphQL behind this scope.
#   [x] repo           Required if any project you want to browse references
#                      PRIVATE repos. Use `public_repo` instead if every repo
#                      is public.
#   [x] read:org       Required so the app can enumerate the organizations
#                      you belong to and surface their Projects v2 boards.
#                      Also required for the v0.2 Workload tab (team
#                      membership resolution + cross-repo search).
#   [x] read:user      Optional. Safe to include.
#
# Do NOT tick any `write:*`, `delete:*`, or `admin:*` scopes — C3PO is
# strictly read-only against GitHub.
#
# SSO note: if your org enforces SAML SSO, after creating the token click
# "Configure SSO" next to it on https://github.com/settings/tokens and
# authorize it for that org. Otherwise org-scoped queries will 401.
#
# The token's identity is the only configuration the app needs. C3PO discovers
# every Projects v2 board you can read across your personal account and every
# org you belong to.
GITHUB_TOKEN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKLOAD_TEAMS — v0.2 Workload tab roster (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of `org/team-slug` entries. Defines which GitHub teams
# the v0.2 Workload tab uses to build its developer roster, and which orgs the
# cross-repo search runs against.
#
# Example:
#   WORKLOAD_TEAMS=lightningnetwork/lnd-maintainers,lightningnetwork/lit-team
#
# Resolution:
#   - The union of members across all listed teams becomes the developer
#     roster shown in the Workload tab's left rail.
#   - The deduplicated set of orgs (from the part before each `/`) becomes
#     the search scope for that developer's open issues + PRs.
#   - Malformed entries are logged as warnings; the rest still resolve.
#
# Permissions: the token must have `read:org` (above) so it can call the
# teams API for every org listed here.
#
# Leave blank to disable the v0.2 Workload tab; v0.1 Sprint Board behavior
# is unaffected.
WORKLOAD_TEAMS=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKLOAD_ORGS — extra orgs to include in workload search (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of GitHub org logins. Use this when your team members
# also contribute to orgs where your token can read repos but CAN'T read team
# membership (e.g. you're an outside collaborator, or the orgs don't expose
# their teams to you).
#
# Example:
#   WORKLOAD_ORGS=other-org,vendor-org
#
# Behavior:
#   - These orgs are unioned with the orgs derived from WORKLOAD_TEAMS and
#     added to the workload search scope. Per-repo counts in the Workload tab
#     will include matching open issues / PRs from these orgs.
#   - The roster (left rail) is still built from WORKLOAD_TEAMS only — this
#     var does NOT add new developers, it just widens where their open work
#     is searched.
#   - Orgs returning zero results are not flagged; the column simply stays
#     empty for everyone.
#
# Permissions: the token needs to be able to see the org's content. No team
# access required. If the org enforces SAML SSO, authorize the token for it.
WORKLOAD_ORGS=
